#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Boots a fresh Silica image in QEMU and checks the base system.

  tools/test-vm [--update VERSION] [--install] [--desktop [--apps] [--appkit]]
                [--gpu virgl|venus] [--keep]

The first boot gets its answers from credentials (locale, keymap, timezone
and a homed user "tester"), so it needs no screen. The checks run as root in
the debug shell on ttyS1, which works only with Secure Boot off.

--update VERSION  serves out/update-VERSION on port 8080, updates, reboots and
                  checks that VERSION booted and was blessed
                  (build it with tools/build-update VERSION).
--install         installs onto a second disk, then boots that disk alone.
--desktop         installs the compositor test extension (out/extensions, from
                  tools/dev-sysext --build-only compositor-tests), starts
                  tester's graphical session on tty2 and checks the compositor
                  on DRM: ready, a client window, frames, the screen, a VT switch.
--apps            with --desktop: also installs compositor-apps (GTK 3, GTK 4 and
                  Qt 6 apps, tools/dev-sysext --build-only compositor-apps) and
                  checks that each maps its window.
--appkit          with --desktop: also installs appkit-dev (tools/dev-sysext
                  --build-only appkit-dev), launches the Kit Gallery and checks
                  that it maps its window and draws it.
--gpu             passes the GPU to tools/run-vm (otherwise software rendering).
--keep            leaves out/vm and the logs in place after a failure.

Logs go to /dev/shm/silica-test-*. Exits non-zero when a check fails.
"""
